   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The scatter plot below shows the age (in years) and the price (in dollars) of used compact cars advertised in the local newspaper.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS AGE IN YEARS ON THE X-AXIS AND PRICE IN DOLLARS ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN DECREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT AND PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (13, 6000) AND (7, 12000).\" height=\"397\" src=\"exercises/media/f860cc6da3b62c80.jpg\" width=\"450\"></p>\n<br> <p dir=\"ltr\">Nora drew a line to fit the data. What is the slope of her line, and what does it mean in the problem?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222486,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"-\\frac1{1000}\">-\\frac1{1000}</span>, for every year older the car is, it decreases <span data-math=\"\\frac1{1000}\">\\frac1{1000}</span> of its value the year before."
